{% set local_problem %}
<p>Priceville's tree coverage varies dramatically from property to property. Newer developments along the highway often have minimal landscaping, but established neighborhoods and rural properties are shaded by mature pines and hardwoods that drop debris year-round.</p>

<p>For many Priceville homeowners, gutter cleaning becomes a dreaded seasonal chore. Climbing ladders multiple times a year isn't just inconvenient — it's risky. And professional cleaning costs $150-200 per visit, adding up to $400-800 annually for homes that need it quarterly.</p>

<p>The bigger concern is what happens between cleanings. When gutters clog during Morgan County's heavy storms, water overflows toward your foundation instead of away from it. On clay soil, that overflow pools and spreads rather than absorbing. Over time, this causes the foundation problems that plague so many local homes.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. Install once, and the cleaning burden — and the overflow risk — is essentially eliminated. As your closest gutter company, we'll help you choose the right system for your specific property.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to flow through while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and other debris. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For Priceville homes, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris, work well with the area's mix of pine and hardwood trees, and are tough enough to withstand heavy debris loads during storms. We'll assess your specific property and recommend the right solution.</p>
{% endset %}

